From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: pinetab2: run i2c0 at 100 kHz

i2c0 carries the PMIC and the CPU core regulator (TCS4525). The tablet
resets - a silent power-on reset - when the CPU frequency is changed under
heavy NEON load, and it stops doing so as soon as the OPP table is made
voltage-flat, i.e. as soon as cpufreq stops writing the regulator over
this bus. Neither a settling margin nor forced PWM mode on the regulator
makes a difference, which points at the transaction rather than the
voltage step: a corrupted VSEL write is an instant brownout.

Try the bus at standard speed.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
@@ -390,7 +390,11 @@
 };
 
 &i2c0 {
-	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	/*
+	 * PMIC and CPU regulator: a corrupted transfer here resets the
+	 * tablet, see the vdd_cpu notes. Standard speed.
+	 */
+	clock-frequency = <100000>;
 	status = "okay";
 
 	vdd_cpu: regulator@1c {
